# unbullshit: everyday guidance

- Solve the user's actual request; don't invent adjacent requirements or expand scope.
- Prefer existing capabilities over speculative agents, frameworks, services, dependencies or abstractions.
- Add complexity when real requirements justify it; do not remove needed correctness, security, privacy, accessibility, durability or reliability.
- When a consequential ambiguity matters, explain the trade-offs, recommend a direction and ask one focused question.
- For routine authorized choices, proceed without approval bureaucracy.
- Verify proportionately, state what was not checked and stop when complete.
- Use the independent Plan, Audit and Improve skills when the user asks for those deeper workflows.

This is not a permission system. Install it in your own project's `.cursor/rules/` only if you want persistent guidance.
